WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.160
Is there a relationship between the faces,

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.760
vertices and edges of a straight face solid?

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.060
Every straight face solids has faces, vertices and edges.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.380
Take the example of a cube.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.620
This is how it's three dimensional view looks like.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.980
We need to find the number of faces,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.920
the number of vertices and the number of edges in a cube.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.620
Let's count the number of faces first.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.160
It has six faces in all.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:36.220
Top and bottom, front and back, left and right.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.460
We write a 6 here.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.560
How many vertices does it have?

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.640
Four at the top and four at the bottom, eight in all.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.640
And how many edges?

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.780
Pause the video and write the number of edges here.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.080
Let's count!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.460
Four horizontal ones at the top,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.480
four vertical ones in the middle

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.140
and four horizontal ones at the bottom.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.160
12 edges in total.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.840
Now here's the important question.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.680
Is there a relation between these three parameters

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.780
of a straight face solid?

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.740
The answer is yes!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.700
For any straight face solid

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.240
if we add its number of faces to its number of vertices

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.580
and then subtract the number of edges,

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.940
we get one special number! And that number is two.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.420
For a cube '6 plus 8 minus 12' gives us '2'.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.900
And this holds true for any straight face solid.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.800
Which are the other straight face solids we know of?

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.060
Cuboid is 1, it looks like this.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.060
A cube is nothing but a special case of a cuboid where the length,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.660
breadth and the height are equal.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.120
So a cuboid also has 6 faces.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.900
8 vertices and 12 edges.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.200
And 'F plus V minus E' will give us 2.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.980
Let's see if it works for other straight face solids.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.420
Do you remember what a square pyramid looks like?

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.180
It is a figure with a square as its base and triangles as its faces.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.060
Square base and 4 triangles as faces.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.360
And what is a triangular prism?

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.500
A prism is a 3 dimensional solid which has identical and parallel ends

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.360
and all flat faces.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.120
A triangular prism would look like this.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.520
It has two identical and parallel triangles at its ends

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.800
and three rectangular faces.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.120
What do we need to find out here?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.440
We need to find the number of faces

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.960
the number of vertices

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.880
and the number of edges in each of the solids

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.980
and see if 'F plus V minus E' will give us 2.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.340
Okay, let's tackle the first solid a square pyramid.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.480
How many faces do you see?

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.140
There are four triangular faces and one square face.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.520
Five in all.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.400
How many vertices?

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.060
One at the top and four at the base!

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.600
Five vertices. And how many edges?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.900
Four slant edges and four edges at the base.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.020
A total of eight edges.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.740
We got F, V and E as 5, 5 and 8 respectively.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.680
And '5 plus 5 minus 8' will give us 2.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.600
So it worked for the square pyramid too.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.820
'F plus V minus E' gave us '2'.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.960
This is called ''Euler's formula''.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.040
For any straight face solid

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.940
'F plus V minus E' will always give us '2'.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.480
Will Euler’s formula work for the triangular prism too ?

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.780
Why don't you give it a try?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.280
Okay, so how many faces?

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.740
Two triangular faces at the ends

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.360
and three rectangular faces in between.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.020
Five faces.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.940
How many vertices?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.300
Three at this end and three at the other, six vertices.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.800
Three edges at the front face

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.520
three in between and three at the back face!

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.560
Nine edges in all.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.360
What will be '5 plus 6 minus 9'?

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.700
Yes, we get a 2.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.900
We will always get a 2.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.920
That's Euler's formula.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.660
‘F plus V minus E’ will always give us a '2'.

